window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7a56f00477a45b74"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"add-evals-to-your-ai-application\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ai\">为 AI 应用添加评测</h1> <p>使用 Codex 将预期行为转化为 Promptfoo 评测套件。</p> <p>请 Codex 检查你的 AI 应用、找出希望评测的行为，并添加一个可运行的 Promptfoo 评测套件。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>已有提示词、模型调用、工具、检索、智能体或产品要求，但还没有可重复运行评测套件的 AI 应用。</li> <li>准备更换模型、提示词、检索设置或智能体，并希望在合并拉取请求前进行回归测试的团队。</li> <li>希望将反复进行的人工检查变成已提交评测用例的质量评审。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/promptfoo/promptfoo/tree/main/plugins/promptfoo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">promptfoo（需联网）</a></td> <td>该插件包含 <code>$promptfoo-evals</code> 和 <code>$promptfoo-provider-setup</code>，用于创建、连接、运行和检查评测套件。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>在改变行为前添加评测</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $promptfoo-evals 为此 AI 应用添加 Promptfoo 评测套件。如果目前还没有可用的 Promptfoo provider 或目标适配器，请先使用 $promptfoo-provider-setup。\n\n要评测的行为：[support answer quality / tool-call correctness / retrieval grounding / business rules / agent task completion]（例如客服回答质量、工具调用正确性、检索依据可靠性、业务规则或智能体任务完成情况）\n\n开始编辑前：\n- 检查用户实际访问的应用路径，以及现有评测或测试。\n- 提出最小但有用的评测方案：目标适配器、初始用例、断言、文件、命令，以及所需的环境变量或本地服务。\n- 基线评测创建并运行之前，不要修改生产提示词、模型设置或应用行为。\n\n要求：\n- 尽可能测试用户实际使用的应用路径，而不只是原始模型提示词。\n- 测试夹具中不得包含密钥、客户数据或敏感个人数据。\n- 添加本地评测命令（例如 `npm run evals`），或说明确切的运行命令。\n\n完成时请提供：\n- 修改的文件\n- 运行的评测命令\n- 通过和失败的用例\n- 建议添加的后续评测\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/configuration/guide/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Promptfoo 配置（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/evaluation-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">评测最佳实践（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>构建 AI 应用或修改现有应用时，你会希望确认它的行为符合预期。评测（evals）可以系统地测试一组场景，并在发布前发现回归问题。</p> <p>你可以使用 Promptfoo 测试 AI 应用，并让 Codex 帮助你创建和维护评测。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用方法</h2> <p>使用 Codex 和 Promptfoo 插件的 <code>$promptfoo-evals</code> 技能，把一种 AI 应用行为变成可重复运行的评测套件。如果应用还没有可用的 Promptfoo 目标，<code>$promptfoo-provider-setup</code> 可以帮助连接评测套件与希望测试的应用路径。</p> <p>Codex 可以检查应用、提出高信号用例、添加 Promptfoo 配置和测试数据、在本地运行评测，并给你一个以后可以继续使用的命令。</p> <p>当要评测的行为具体明确时，这种用例效果最好：例如客服回答质量、检索依据、分类标签、工具调用、JSON 结构、业务规则，或提示词与模型迁移的可靠性。</p> <p>一个好的第一版应是便于审查的代码和测试数据：<code>promptfooconfig.yaml</code> 或等价配置、一个小型 <code>evals/</code> 目录、测试用例、调用目标应用所需的适配器，以及类似 <code>npm run evals</code> 的本地命令。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-what-to-evaluate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">选择评测对象</h2> <p>从一项用户可见的承诺开始。不要一次要求 Codex 评测整个 AI 系统。较小的套件更容易建立信任、检查并持续运行。</p> <p>好的首个目标包括：</p> <ul> <li><strong>正确性：</strong> 分类、提取、总结、路由或转换。</li> <li><strong>依据可靠性：</strong> 答案是否始终与检索到的文档或引用来源保持一致。</li> <li><strong>工具使用：</strong> 是否选择正确工具、传入有效参数，并妥善处理工具错误。</li> <li><strong>格式或业务规则：</strong> JSON Schema、字段名、业务规则限制，或面向 UI 的文案约定。</li> <li><strong>提示词或模型迁移：</strong> 确认新的提示词、模型、系统消息或检索设置不会破坏重要用例。</li> </ul> <p>从产品要求、错误报告、支持升级工单或经过脱敏且适合提交到代码仓库的示例开始。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-for-an-eval-plan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">请求评测方案</h2> <p>在 Codex 编辑之前，请它检查项目并给出包含目标路径、固件、断言、适配器和命令的方案。这样你有机会发现测试目标不对或用例信号太弱的问题。</p> <p>评审方案时，应确认它写明 Promptfoo 将调用的应用路径或端点、首批种子用例、断言、要创建的文件、本地命令，以及需要的密钥或服务。如果方案测试的是原始模型而不是用户实际访问的应用路径，请问 Codex 这是否是有意为之。</p> <p><a id=\"implement-run-and-iterate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">实施、运行并迭代</h2> <p>方案正确后，让 Codex 实施。第一版应尽量简单：配置、用例、固件、必要时的目标适配器、本地命令，以及命令实际运行成功的证据。</p> <p>基于应用的小型评测套件可以采用以下结构：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">evals/\n  promptfooconfig.yaml\n  tests/\n    cases.yaml\n  providers/\n    provider.js  # only if the built-in provider cannot call the app directly\n</code></pre> <p>先在更改行为前运行评测。基线可以告诉你应用原本是否就会失败、断言是否需要调整，或目标适配器是否配置错误。调整过于脆弱或含糊的断言，但要让真正的产品失败继续可见。</p> <p>以后每次更改前都可以用此套件进行比较。每当错误、发布要求或产品评审揭示了你想持续守护的行为，就增加新的用例。等本地命令稳定后，再考虑将它加入 CI 或发布清单。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"add-evals-to-your-ai-application\">Add evals to your AI application</h1> <p>Use Codex to turn expected behavior into a Promptfoo eval suite.</p> <p>Ask Codex to inspect your AI application, identify the behavior you want to evaluate, and add a runnable Promptfoo eval suite.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>AI applications that already have prompts, model calls, tools, retrieval, agents, or product requirements but no repeatable eval suite.</li> <li>Teams preparing a model, prompt, retrieval, or agent change and wanting regression tests before the pull request merges.</li> <li>Quality reviews where repeated manual checks should become committed eval cases.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/promptfoo/promptfoo/tree/main/plugins/promptfoo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">promptfoo (online)</a></td> <td>Plugin that includes <code>$promptfoo-evals</code> and <code>$promptfoo-provider-setup</code> for creating, connecting, running, and QAing eval suites.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Add Evals Before You Change Behavior</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $promptfoo-evals to add a Promptfoo eval suite for this AI application. If there is not already a working Promptfoo provider or target adapter, use $promptfoo-provider-setup first.\n\nBehavior to evaluate: [support answer quality / tool-call correctness / retrieval grounding / business rules / agent task completion]\n\nBefore editing:\n- Inspect the app path users hit and any existing evals or tests.\n- Propose the smallest useful eval plan: target adapter, seed cases, assertions, files, commands, and required env vars or local services.\n- Do not change production prompts, model settings, or app behavior until the baseline eval exists and has been run.\n\nRequirements:\n- Exercise the application path users hit when possible, not only the raw model prompt.\n- Keep fixtures free of secrets, customer data, and sensitive personal data.\n- Add a local eval command such as `npm run evals` or document the exact command to run.\n\nFinish with:\n- Files changed\n- Eval commands run\n- Passing and failing cases\n- Recommended next evals to add\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/configuration/guide/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Promptfoo configuration (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/evaluation-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Evaluation best practices (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When you are building an AI application, or making changes to an existing one, you want to make sure it behaves as expected. Evals are a way to systematically test a set of scenarios and catch regressions before they ship.</p> <p>You can use Promptfoo to run evals on your AI application, and Codex to help you create and maintain the evals.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <p>Use Codex with the Promptfoo plugin's <code>$promptfoo-evals</code> skill to turn one AI app behavior into a repeatable eval suite. When the app does not already have a working Promptfoo target, <code>$promptfoo-provider-setup</code> helps connect the suite to the application path you want to test.</p> <p>Codex can inspect the app, propose high-signal cases, add the Promptfoo config and test data, run the suite locally, and give you a command to keep using.</p> <p>This use case works best when the behavior is concrete: support answer quality, retrieval grounding, classifier labels, tool calls, JSON shape, business rules, or prompt and model migration confidence.</p> <p>A strong first pass should be reviewable code and test data: a <code>promptfooconfig.yaml</code> or equivalent config, a small <code>evals/</code> directory, test cases, any target adapter needed to call the app, and a local command such as <code>npm run evals</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-what-to-evaluate\">Choose what to evaluate</h2> <p>Start with one user-visible promise. Avoid asking Codex to evaluate the entire AI system in one pass. A smaller suite is easier to trust, review, and keep running.</p> <p>Good first targets include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Correctness:</strong> classification, extraction, summarization, routing, or transformation.</li> <li><strong>Grounding:</strong> answers that should stay tied to retrieved documents or cited sources.</li> <li><strong>Tool use:</strong> choosing the right tool, passing valid arguments, and handling tool errors.</li> <li><strong>Format or business rules:</strong> JSON schemas, field names, business-rule limits, or UI-facing copy contracts.</li> <li><strong>Prompt or model migration:</strong> making sure a new prompt, model, system message, or retrieval setting does not break important cases.</li> </ul> <p>Start from product requirements, bug reports, support escalations, or sanitized examples your team is comfortable committing to the repo.</p> <h2 id=\"ask-for-an-eval-plan\">Ask for an eval plan</h2> <p>Codex should inspect before it edits. Ask for a plan that names the target path, fixtures, assertions, adapter, and commands. This gives you a chance to catch the wrong target or weak test cases before files are added.</p> <p>Review the plan before implementation. It should name the app path or endpoint Promptfoo will call, the first seed cases, the assertions, the files Codex will create, the local command, and any required secrets or services. If the plan tests the raw model instead of the application path users hit, ask Codex whether that is intentional.</p> <h2 id=\"implement-run-and-iterate\">Implement, run, and iterate</h2> <p>Once the plan is correct, ask Codex to implement it. The first implementation should be boring: config, cases, fixtures, a target adapter if needed, a command, and proof that the command ran.</p> <p>A small app-backed suite might look like this:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">evals/\n  promptfooconfig.yaml\n  tests/\n    cases.yaml\n  providers/\n    provider.js  # only if the built-in provider cannot call the app directly\n</code></pre> <p>Run the suite before changing behavior. The baseline tells you whether the app already fails the cases, whether the assertions need tuning, or whether the target adapter is wrong. Tune assertions when they are too brittle or vague, but keep real product failures visible.</p> <p>After the first run, use the suite to compare app changes before they ship. Add new cases whenever a bug, launch requirement, or product review shows behavior you want to keep stable. Once the local command is stable, ask Codex to add it to CI or your release checklist.</p>"};
